{
  "checked": "Every line here is checked by the tests named under it, on every change to AI Juggler. A line without a test can't be added.",
  "groups": [
    {
      "id": "reads",
      "title": "What it reads, on your Mac only",
      "claims": [
        {
          "id": "no-credentials",
          "text": "It never reads your passwords, tokens or API keys, or the tools' Keychain items. It reads only whether you're signed in, and as which account: its email and organisation.",
          "tests": [
            "crates/juggler-app/tests/no_bare_tools.rs::no_sign_in_file_is_read",
            "crates/juggler-adapters/tests/claude_code_adapter.rs::login_state_is_metadata_only",
            "crates/juggler-adapters/tests/scan.rs::scan_code_never_reads_credential_contents",
            "crates/juggler-app/tests/environment_scan_no_cli.rs::the_environment_scan_runs_no_vendor_cli"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "settings-parts",
          "text": "From Claude Code's settings.json it reads only the settings it needs, each one named in its code and checked.",
          "tests": [
            "crates/juggler-app/tests/no_bare_tools.rs::no_sign_in_file_is_read"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "native-crash-reports",
          "text": "With crash reports on, it looks through macOS's new crash reports for AI Juggler's own, and keeps only what failed and where.",
          "tests": [
            "crates/juggler-app/src/crash_native.rs::an_ips_crash_keeps_its_kind_and_frames_and_nothing_else",
            "crates/juggler-app/src/crash_native.rs::only_crashes_after_the_first_look_are_kept_and_never_reads_nothing",
            "crates/juggler-app/src/crash_native.rs::links_and_oversized_files_are_not_read"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "other-managers",
          "text": "If you use Claude Squad or Vibe Kanban, it reads their own lists for which repository each of their worktrees belongs to and which config folders their profiles use, and nothing else they keep. It never opens their sign-in or key files.",
          "tests": [
            "crates/juggler-adapters/tests/other_managers.rs::claude_squad_worktrees_come_with_their_repositories",
            "crates/juggler-adapters/tests/other_managers.rs::vibe_kanban_profiles_offer_the_folders_they_point_at",
            "crates/juggler-adapters/tests/other_managers.rs::the_importers_never_name_a_sign_in_or_key_file"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "open-sessions",
          "text": "To show what's open, it reads each tool's own session files: Claude Code's list of running sessions, and from the Claude app only each session's ids, folder, title, times, archived mark and status word, never its summaries. For the Codex app it reads which of its files the app has open. It never reads a running program's environment, where the Claude app keeps a sign-in token.",
          "tests": [
            "crates/juggler-app/tests/trust.rs::no_process_environment_is_ever_read",
            "crates/juggler-app/src/features/conversations/procs.rs::the_process_read_never_asks_for_environments",
            "crates/juggler-adapters/src/claude_live.rs::an_app_session_keeps_its_status_word_and_never_its_summary_text",
            "crates/juggler-adapters/src/claude_live.rs::a_pid_file_reads_its_session_and_the_key_file_is_never_listed",
            "crates/juggler-adapters/src/codex_live.rs::held_locks_and_rollouts_name_their_threads_once"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "parent-chain",
          "text": "To know which app and profile a session runs in, it reads the names of running programs, the apps that started them and the options they started with, on your Mac only, and never their environment.",
          "tests": [
            "crates/juggler-app/src/features/conversations/places.rs::a_desktop_session_is_in_its_claude_instance_by_its_argument",
            "crates/juggler-app/src/features/conversations/places.rs::a_terminal_session_is_in_its_terminal_and_an_unknown_app_by_its_name",
            "crates/juggler-app/tests/trust.rs::no_process_environment_is_ever_read"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "app-icons",
          "text": "To show apps' icons, AI Juggler reads the icon from each app installed on your Mac; nothing is sent or copied elsewhere. It reads only inside the app itself, and keeps a small copy in its own folder until the app changes.",
          "tests": [
            "crates/juggler-app/src/features/app_icons/tests.rs::only_an_app_folder_that_is_not_a_link_is_read",
            "crates/juggler-app/src/features/app_icons/tests.rs::a_bundle_whose_icon_or_plist_links_out_of_it_is_refused",
            "crates/juggler-app/src/features/app_icons/tests.rs::an_app_is_found_by_its_place_its_id_or_its_folder_and_never_otherwise",
            "crates/juggler-app/src/features/app_icons/tests.rs::an_icon_is_kept_until_the_app_changes_then_read_again",
            "crates/juggler-app/tests/trust.rs::the_app_reaches_only_its_own_addresses"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "this-mac-other-apps",
          "text": "To show what else is using memory, This Mac names the biggest other apps by their app or program name, with their memory. It never shows their folders or the options they started with, and it can't stop them.",
          "tests": [
            "crates/juggler-app/src/machine_memory.rs::other_apps_show_names_never_paths",
            "crates/juggler-supervisor/src/live_stats.rs::other_processes_carry_a_name_and_memory_only_and_leave_ai_juggler_out",
            "ui/src/screens/this-mac-page.test.tsx::shows the whole Mac's memory, explains pressure, and lists what else uses it by name, read-only",
            "crates/juggler-app/tests/trust.rs::no_process_environment_is_ever_read"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "last-messages",
          "text": "A session's last messages are read from the end of its transcript on your Mac while its page is open, and kept nowhere. One switch in Settings › Desktop apps turns them off.",
          "tests": [
            "ui/src/screens/settings/desktop-apps.test.tsx::Last messages are on until you turn them off, and only off is kept",
            "ui/src/pages/session/last-messages.test.tsx::are read only once the page is shown, and once",
            "ui/src/pages/session/last-messages.test.tsx::a paired Mac's session is never read here",
            "crates/juggler-adapters/src/last_turns.rs::only_the_end_is_read_and_a_cut_line_is_skipped",
            "crates/juggler-app/src/features/conversations/last_messages.rs::an_api_key_in_a_turn_shows_redacted",
            "crates/juggler-app/src/features/conversations/last_messages.rs::a_private_key_block_is_taken_out_whole",
            "crates/juggler-app/src/features/conversations/last_messages.rs::nothing_is_kept_written_or_logged",
            "crates/juggler-app/src/features/conversations/last_messages.rs::off_in_settings_no_transcript_is_looked_up_or_read"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "changes",
      "title": "What it changes",
      "claims": [
        {
          "id": "own-folder",
          "text": "What it keeps lives in its own folder, ~/Library/Application Support/AI Juggler (AI Juggler Nightly for Nightly), and in its own Keychain items.",
          "tests": [
